{
  "version": 1,
  "_note": "V03 - Core/Clerk inline auth surfaces (architecture/proposals/inline-native-surfaces.md). The same law as stripe.json: the module owns the sign-in ATTEMPT, and the overlay face (dsx.module.clerk.authview, the vendor's presented sheet) and the component face (<clerk.SignIn/> and friends) are two views onto it. Two attempt models that disagree is a user signed in on one face and stuck on a password screen on the other, so a second submit while one is in flight is refused `busy`. ladder[] is what an inline auth form puts on screen for the status the vendor last reported: a wrong password is NOT terminal, and an unknown status degrades to a restart with a code rather than to a form with no fields.",
  "sessionRef": {
    "_note": "The security boundary for <clerk.SignIn/> session=. Clerk's publishable key is a pk_ token, so a literal one is refused AND named - the family only sharpens the message, the allowlist is what does the refusing. A Clerk session id (sess_...) parses as a bare word and is refused just as hard, which is the whole point: the rule accepts reference SHAPES, not values that look safe.",
    "kinds": [
      "implicit",
      "module-context",
      "store-var",
      "global",
      "config",
      "attribute",
      "scope"
    ],
    "refusals": [
      "missing_reference",
      "literal_secret",
      "literal_value",
      "compound_template",
      "unknown_reference"
    ],
    "families": [
      "publishable_key",
      "secret_key"
    ],
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "omitted binds the module's current attempt",
        "value": null,
        "expect": {
          "kind": "implicit",
          "path": ""
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "the canonical module-context reference",
        "value": "dsx.module.clerk.context.session",
        "expect": {
          "kind": "module-context",
          "path": "dsx.module.clerk.context.session"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "a store variable holding the attempt handle",
        "value": "dsx.variable.signIn",
        "expect": {
          "kind": "store-var",
          "path": "dsx.variable.signIn"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "a config value, for a build-time attempt binding",
        "value": "{{ dsx.config.clerkSession }}",
        "expect": {
          "kind": "config",
          "path": "dsx.config.clerkSession"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "an empty attribute is an author mistake",
        "value": "",
        "expect": {
          "error": "missing_reference"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "a publishable key is refused, and named",
        "value": "pk_live_fixture_640ccdbe",
        "expect": {
          "error": "literal_secret",
          "family": "publishable_key"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "a secret key is refused, and named",
        "value": "sk_live_fixture_486afff1",
        "expect": {
          "error": "literal_secret",
          "family": "secret_key"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "a Clerk session id is refused as hard as a key",
        "value": "sess_2abcDEF456",
        "expect": {
          "error": "unknown_reference"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "a JWT template value is refused",
        "value": "https://example.clerk.accounts.dev/v1/client",
        "expect": {
          "error": "literal_value"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "two interpolations are not one reference",
        "value": "{{ dsx.variable.a }}{{ dsx.variable.b }}",
        "expect": {
          "error": "compound_template"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "machine": {
    "_note": "One sign-in attempt, two views. `start` is a factor SUBMIT, `fail` is a rejected credential and is NOT terminal (an app that tells a user their password is wrong and then refuses to let them try another is the bug this pins), `cancel` while submitting abandons the submit and keeps the attempt, and `cancel` with nothing in flight abandons the ATTEMPT, which is terminal.",
    "views": [
      "overlay",
      "inline"
    ],
    "states": [
      "idle",
      "ready",
      "confirming",
      "succeeded",
      "failed",
      "canceled"
    ],
    "refusals": [
      "already_open",
      "not_ready",
      "busy",
      "settled",
      "not_confirming",
      "detached_view"
    ],
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "the inline form alone: open, attach, submit, signed in",
        "steps": [
          {
            "op": "open"
          },
          {
            "op": "attach",
            "view": "inline"
          },
          {
            "op": "start",
            "view": "inline"
          },
          {
            "op": "complete"
          }
        ],
        "expect": [
          {
            "state": "ready",
            "notify": [],
            "attempts": 0
          },
          {
            "state": "ready",
            "notify": [],
            "attempts": 0
          },
          {
            "state": "confirming",
            "notify": [
              "inline"
            ],
            "attempts": 1,
            "by": "inline"
          },
          {
            "state": "succeeded",
            "notify": [
              "inline"
            ],
            "attempts": 1,
            "outcome": "succeeded",
            "by": "inline"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "started in the sheet, finished inline - ONE attempt, both faces told",
        "steps": [
          {
            "op": "open"
          },
          {
            "op": "attach",
            "view": "overlay"
          },
          {
            "op": "attach",
            "view": "inline"
          },
          {
            "op": "start",
            "view": "overlay"
          },
          {
            "op": "complete"
          }
        ],
        "expect": [
          {
            "state": "ready",
            "notify": [],
            "attempts": 0
          },
          {
            "state": "ready",
            "notify": [],
            "attempts": 0
          },
          {
            "state": "ready",
            "notify": [],
            "attempts": 0
          },
          {
            "state": "confirming",
            "notify": [
              "overlay",
              "inline"
            ],
            "attempts": 1,
            "by": "overlay"
          },
          {
            "state": "succeeded",
            "notify": [
              "overlay",
              "inline"
            ],
            "attempts": 1,
            "outcome": "succeeded",
            "by": "overlay"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "THE DOUBLE-SUBMIT GUARD: a second submit while one is in flight is refused",
        "steps": [
          {
            "op": "open"
          },
          {
            "op": "attach",
            "view": "inline"
          },
          {
            "op": "start",
            "view": "inline"
          },
          {
            "op": "start",
            "view": "inline"
          },
          {
            "op": "complete"
          }
        ],
        "expect": [
          {
            "state": "ready",
            "notify": [],
            "attempts": 0
          },
          {
            "state": "ready",
            "notify": [],
            "attempts": 0
          },
          {
            "state": "confirming",
            "notify": [
              "inline"
            ],
            "attempts": 1,
            "by": "inline"
          },
          {
            "error": "busy",
            "state": "confirming"
          },
          {
            "state": "succeeded",
            "notify": [
              "inline"
            ],
            "attempts": 1,
            "outcome": "succeeded",
            "by": "inline"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "a wrong password is retryable: the attempt survives",
        "steps": [
          {
            "op": "open"
          },
          {
            "op": "attach",
            "view": "inline"
          },
          {
            "op": "start",
            "view": "inline"
          },
          {
            "op": "fail",
            "code": "form_password_incorrect"
          },
          {
            "op": "start",
            "view": "inline"
          },
          {
            "op": "complete"
          }
        ],
        "expect": [
          {
            "state": "ready",
            "notify": [],
            "attempts": 0
          },
          {
            "state": "ready",
            "notify": [],
            "attempts": 0
          },
          {
            "state": "confirming",
            "notify": [
              "inline"
            ],
            "attempts": 1,
            "by": "inline"
          },
          {
            "state": "failed",
            "notify": [
              "inline"
            ],
            "attempts": 1,
            "outcome": "failed",
            "by": "inline",
            "code": "form_password_incorrect"
          },
          {
            "state": "confirming",
            "notify": [
              "inline"
            ],
            "attempts": 2,
            "by": "inline"
          },
          {
            "state": "succeeded",
            "notify": [
              "inline"
            ],
            "attempts": 2,
            "outcome": "succeeded",
            "by": "inline"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "the form unmounts mid-submit and is STILL told the outcome",
        "steps": [
          {
            "op": "open"
          },
          {
            "op": "attach",
            "view": "inline"
          },
          {
            "op": "start",
            "view": "inline"
          },
          {
            "op": "detach",
            "view": "inline"
          },
          {
            "op": "fail",
            "code": "form_password_incorrect"
          }
        ],
        "expect": [
          {
            "state": "ready",
            "notify": [],
            "attempts": 0
          },
          {
            "state": "ready",
            "notify": [],
            "attempts": 0
          },
          {
            "state": "confirming",
            "notify": [
              "inline"
            ],
            "attempts": 1,
            "by": "inline"
          },
          {
            "state": "confirming",
            "notify": [],
            "attempts": 1
          },
          {
            "state": "failed",
            "notify": [
              "inline"
            ],
            "attempts": 1,
            "outcome": "failed",
            "by": "inline",
            "code": "form_password_incorrect"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "abandoning the attempt is terminal, and reopening is refused",
        "steps": [
          {
            "op": "open"
          },
          {
            "op": "attach",
            "view": "inline"
          },
          {
            "op": "cancel"
          },
          {
            "op": "open"
          }
        ],
        "expect": [
          {
            "state": "ready",
            "notify": [],
            "attempts": 0
          },
          {
            "state": "ready",
            "notify": [],
            "attempts": 0
          },
          {
            "state": "canceled",
            "notify": [
              "inline"
            ],
            "attempts": 0,
            "outcome": "canceled"
          },
          {
            "error": "settled",
            "state": "canceled"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "a second factor is another submit on the SAME attempt",
        "steps": [
          {
            "op": "open"
          },
          {
            "op": "attach",
            "view": "inline"
          },
          {
            "op": "start",
            "view": "inline"
          },
          {
            "op": "fail",
            "code": "needs_second_factor"
          },
          {
            "op": "start",
            "view": "inline"
          },
          {
            "op": "complete"
          }
        ],
        "expect": [
          {
            "state": "ready",
            "notify": [],
            "attempts": 0
          },
          {
            "state": "ready",
            "notify": [],
            "attempts": 0
          },
          {
            "state": "confirming",
            "notify": [
              "inline"
            ],
            "attempts": 1,
            "by": "inline"
          },
          {
            "state": "failed",
            "notify": [
              "inline"
            ],
            "attempts": 1,
            "outcome": "failed",
            "by": "inline",
            "code": "needs_second_factor"
          },
          {
            "state": "confirming",
            "notify": [
              "inline"
            ],
            "attempts": 2,
            "by": "inline"
          },
          {
            "state": "succeeded",
            "notify": [
              "inline"
            ],
            "attempts": 2,
            "outcome": "succeeded",
            "by": "inline"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "submitting before the module opened an attempt is not_ready",
        "steps": [
          {
            "op": "start",
            "view": "inline"
          }
        ],
        "expect": [
          {
            "error": "not_ready",
            "state": "idle"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "ladder": {
    "_note": "One rung of a vendor sign-in attempt, as an inline component renders it. The vendor owns the attempt; this decides only what is on screen for the status the vendor last reported. Strategy order puts the cheapest gesture first (a passkey beats a password beats a code the user has to go and fetch), unknown strategies are KEPT and sorted after the known ones so a vendor adding one next quarter still renders it, and an unknown STATUS restarts with a code rather than rendering an empty form.",
    "steps": [
      "identifier",
      "first_factor",
      "second_factor",
      "new_password",
      "requirements",
      "complete",
      "restart"
    ],
    "strategyOrder": [
      "passkey",
      "password",
      "email_code",
      "phone_code",
      "email_link",
      "reset_password_email_code"
    ],
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "the first rung asks for the identifier",
        "input": {
          "status": "needs_identifier",
          "strategies": [
            "password",
            "email_code"
          ],
          "missing": []
        },
        "expect": {
          "step": "identifier",
          "fields": [
            "identifier"
          ],
          "strategies": [
            "password",
            "email_code"
          ],
          "terminal": false,
          "code": ""
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "a password account shows a password field",
        "input": {
          "status": "needs_first_factor",
          "strategies": [
            "password",
            "email_code"
          ],
          "missing": []
        },
        "expect": {
          "step": "first_factor",
          "fields": [
            "password"
          ],
          "strategies": [
            "password",
            "email_code"
          ],
          "terminal": false,
          "code": ""
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "a passwordless account shows the code field instead",
        "input": {
          "status": "needs_first_factor",
          "strategies": [
            "email_code",
            "phone_code"
          ],
          "missing": []
        },
        "expect": {
          "step": "first_factor",
          "fields": [
            "code"
          ],
          "strategies": [
            "email_code",
            "phone_code"
          ],
          "terminal": false,
          "code": ""
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "the second factor is always a code",
        "input": {
          "status": "needs_second_factor",
          "strategies": [
            "phone_code",
            "totp"
          ],
          "missing": []
        },
        "expect": {
          "step": "second_factor",
          "fields": [
            "code"
          ],
          "strategies": [
            "phone_code",
            "totp"
          ],
          "terminal": false,
          "code": ""
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "a forced reset asks twice",
        "input": {
          "status": "needs_new_password",
          "strategies": [
            "password"
          ],
          "missing": []
        },
        "expect": {
          "step": "new_password",
          "fields": [
            "password",
            "confirmation"
          ],
          "strategies": [
            "password"
          ],
          "terminal": false,
          "code": ""
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "sign-up requirements come from the vendor",
        "input": {
          "status": "missing_requirements",
          "strategies": [
            "password"
          ],
          "missing": [
            "email_address",
            "username"
          ]
        },
        "expect": {
          "step": "requirements",
          "fields": [
            "email_address",
            "username"
          ],
          "strategies": [
            "password"
          ],
          "terminal": false,
          "code": ""
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "requirements with nothing named fall back to the identifier",
        "input": {
          "status": "missing_requirements",
          "strategies": [
            "password"
          ],
          "missing": []
        },
        "expect": {
          "step": "requirements",
          "fields": [
            "identifier"
          ],
          "strategies": [
            "password"
          ],
          "terminal": false,
          "code": ""
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "complete is terminal and has no fields",
        "input": {
          "status": "complete",
          "strategies": [
            "password"
          ],
          "missing": []
        },
        "expect": {
          "step": "complete",
          "fields": [],
          "strategies": [
            "password"
          ],
          "terminal": true,
          "code": ""
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "abandoned is terminal and restarts",
        "input": {
          "status": "abandoned",
          "strategies": [
            "password"
          ],
          "missing": []
        },
        "expect": {
          "step": "restart",
          "fields": [],
          "strategies": [
            "password"
          ],
          "terminal": true,
          "code": ""
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "a status this build does not know restarts, and says so",
        "input": {
          "status": "needs_teleport",
          "strategies": [
            "password"
          ],
          "missing": []
        },
        "expect": {
          "step": "restart",
          "fields": [],
          "strategies": [
            "password"
          ],
          "terminal": false,
          "code": "unknown_status"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "strategy order is the ladder's, not the vendor's",
        "input": {
          "status": "needs_first_factor",
          "strategies": [
            "email_link",
            "password",
            "passkey",
            "phone_code"
          ],
          "missing": []
        },
        "expect": {
          "step": "first_factor",
          "fields": [
            "password"
          ],
          "strategies": [
            "passkey",
            "password",
            "phone_code",
            "email_link"
          ],
          "terminal": false,
          "code": ""
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "unknown strategies are kept, sorted, and put after the known ones",
        "input": {
          "status": "needs_first_factor",
          "strategies": [
            "oauth_google",
            "password",
            "oauth_apple",
            "totp"
          ],
          "missing": []
        },
        "expect": {
          "step": "first_factor",
          "fields": [
            "password"
          ],
          "strategies": [
            "password",
            "oauth_apple",
            "oauth_google",
            "totp"
          ],
          "terminal": false,
          "code": ""
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "duplicates collapse",
        "input": {
          "status": "needs_first_factor",
          "strategies": [
            "password",
            "password",
            "email_code"
          ],
          "missing": []
        },
        "expect": {
          "step": "first_factor",
          "fields": [
            "password"
          ],
          "strategies": [
            "password",
            "email_code"
          ],
          "terminal": false,
          "code": ""
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "no strategies at all is still a real rung",
        "input": {
          "status": "needs_first_factor",
          "strategies": [],
          "missing": []
        },
        "expect": {
          "step": "first_factor",
          "fields": [
            "code"
          ],
          "strategies": [],
          "terminal": false,
          "code": ""
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "retain": {
    "_note": "Keyed identity. An auth form holds a half-typed identifier and a vendor attempt handle; rebuilding it on an unrelated re-render loses both and reads to the user as the app forgetting what they typed.",
    "keys": [
      {
        "name": "an explicit key wins outright",
        "input": {
          "tag": "clerk.SignIn",
          "key": "login",
          "session": "dsx.module.clerk.context.session",
          "index": 0
        },
        "expect": "clerk.SignIn#login"
      },
      {
        "name": "no key derives from tag, session reference and position",
        "input": {
          "tag": "clerk.UserProfile",
          "session": "dsx.variable.signIn",
          "index": 1
        },
        "expect": "clerk.UserProfile@dsx.variable.signIn[1]"
      },
      {
        "name": "the implicit session still derives a stable key",
        "input": {
          "tag": "clerk.UserButton",
          "index": 0
        },
        "expect": "clerk.UserButton@[0]"
      }
    ]
  },
  "session": {
    "_note": "A2 - THE CONTEXT PROJECTION. Given a vendor session/user snapshot, what each of the twelve declared context vars reads. This is the fold that keeps three lanes from drifting on the plane the whole A2 plan depends on: `<DSXView/>` markup binds dsx.module.clerk.context.signedIn with no web view anywhere in the build, so the three renderers must agree on what `signed in` MEANS. THE THREE LAWS pinned here. (1) NO SESSION, NO IDENTITY: a signed-out client publishes empty for every identity var even when the lane still holds a cached User object - a stale name on screen after sign-out is the leak this row exists to stop. (2) A PENDING TASK IS NOT SIGNED IN: Clerk returns a session in `pending` status carrying tasks[] when the instance forces MFA or organization selection; that session has an id and a user and is NOT usable, so signedIn stays false while sessionId/userId/pendingTask are published - the app can render the task rather than a dashboard the API will refuse. (3) AN UNKNOWN TASK IS `unknown`, NEVER EMPTY: a task key this build has never heard of must not read as `no task pending`, for the same reason the sign-in ladder degrades to `restart` and not to an empty form. The task keys are the vendor's own raw wire strings and are BYTE-IDENTICAL on all three SDKs: ClerkKit Session.Task.rawValue, clerk-android SessionTask.key, and clerk-js SessionTask['key'] all spell them choose-organization / setup-mfa / reset-password. The map carries the UNDERSCORE and `mfa-required` spellings beside the hyphen ones and the lookup lowercases first, because clerk-android's own `SessionTaskKey.fromRaw` normalises all of them: a fold that only knew the hyphen form would answer `unknown` on Android for a task the vendor itself resolves.",
    "vars": [
      "signedIn",
      "userId",
      "sessionId",
      "email",
      "name",
      "imageUrl",
      "orgId",
      "orgRole",
      "orgSlug",
      "pendingTask",
      "loaded",
      "lastError"
    ],
    "tasks": [
      "",
      "chooseOrganization",
      "setupMFA",
      "resetPassword",
      "unknown"
    ],
    "taskKeys": {
      "choose-organization": "chooseOrganization",
      "choose_organization": "chooseOrganization",
      "setup-mfa": "setupMFA",
      "setup_mfa": "setupMFA",
      "mfa-required": "setupMFA",
      "mfa_required": "setupMFA",
      "reset-password": "resetPassword",
      "reset_password": "resetPassword"
    },
    "signedInStatus": "active",
    "secretVars": [],
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "nothing loaded yet reads empty, not signed out",
        "input": {},
        "expect": {
          "signedIn": false,
          "userId": "",
          "sessionId": "",
          "email": "",
          "name": "",
          "imageUrl": "",
          "orgId": "",
          "orgRole": "",
          "orgSlug": "",
          "pendingTask": "",
          "loaded": false,
          "lastError": ""
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "loaded and signed out: every identity var is empty",
        "input": {
          "loaded": true
        },
        "expect": {
          "signedIn": false,
          "userId": "",
          "sessionId": "",
          "email": "",
          "name": "",
          "imageUrl": "",
          "orgId": "",
          "orgRole": "",
          "orgSlug": "",
          "pendingTask": "",
          "loaded": true,
          "lastError": ""
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "a signed-in personal account, no organization",
        "input": {
          "loaded": true,
